Package: tidydiversity
Title: Taxonomic, Phylogenetic and Functional Diversity with Tidy Hill Numbers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: Tidy, pipe-friendly tools for estimating taxonomic,
    phylogenetic and functional diversity from long-format community data.
    All three dimensions are expressed as Hill numbers of the same order q
    (effective numbers of species), following Chao, Chiu and Jost (2014)
    <doi:10.1146/annurev-ecolsys-120213-091540> and Chao et al. (2019)
    <doi:10.1002/ecm.1343>. Computes observed and asymptotic diversity,
    sample coverage, and size- and coverage-based rarefaction and
    extrapolation following Chao et al. (2014) <doi:10.1890/13-0133.1>, and
    partitions beta diversity into turnover and nestedness components
    following Baselga (2010) <doi:10.1111/j.1466-8238.2009.00490.x>. Every
    function takes a data frame and returns a tibble, uses data-masking for
    column arguments, and supports grouped data and the '.by' argument.
